; The HUD's one Theme (plan row P58, Michael's decision of 2026-10-15): the look of the HUD's
; Controls lives here, so a new look is this file alone (STYLE.md "Reskin"). It holds the fonts,
; the font sizes, the command bar chip's backdrop, the HUD v2 tokens and accent pairs (P118, ADR
; 0025 section 13) and the colours of the selection box and anchor. The text and button colours
; and the Button StyleBoxes are the engine's defaults and are not in this file: a restyle adds
; them here (Label/colors/font_color, Button/styles/normal) with no code change. main.tscn sets
; the theme on the Controls under Hud (Hud/SafeArea and Hud/BoxOverlay); every Control below
; inherits it, and so does a HUD root added later with this theme on it. A new font goes under
; assets/art/fonts/ (CREDITS.md row; its licence text beside every build (P118b) and, from
; Phase 5's settings on, in its Licences screen) and is referenced from here only: the scan of
; tests/project/test_ui_theme_scan.gd flags a font named in any other script, scene or resource.
; The backdrop has a palette row in STYLE.md ("HUD panel backdrop"); this file is its value of
; record. BoxOverlay's fill and outline are also FeedbackStyle.FILL and OUTLINE, which the
; world-space move markers draw with (game/view): a new palette changes both.
;
; Fonts (P605, ADR 0049 amendment of 2026-11-25, SIL OFL 1.1, the unmodified upstream files of
; assets/art/fonts/): Michael's Figma type, three faces. Inter is the body face (Regular as the
; theme's default font) and the button face (Bold: CapsButton). IBM Plex Mono Regular is the label
; and number face (NumberLabel, ItemCost, PowerNumber). Roboto Condensed Bold is the display face of
; titles and headings (CapsTitle, CapsBigTitle, MenuTitle, AttackTitle, the side names) and, being
; the narrow one, of the names and words on the tight cards and tabs (ItemCaption, ItemSash, PillWord:
; Inter at 14 dp was 2 to 3 % too wide for the 102 dp card). Plex Mono's digits are fixed width, but the digits of a number that changes keep their
; fixed slots in code for now (P119; P618 may drop them). The titles and buttons are upper case
; written in the text itself, each in its own FontVariation whose spacing_glyph is the tracking in
; whole base px: the dp step turns the font size into px and leaves the tracking. ADR 0025 section
; 13 asks 6 to 14 % of the size. One whole-px tracking cannot hold that over the profiles' dp-to-px
; ratios of 1.0 to 2.37, so it is held on the phones (ratios 1.75 to 2.37) and not on the tablet or
; the desktop window, which sit above the band; tests/ui/test_ui_theme_fonts.gd pins all three. The
; tracking entries are listed in metadata/base_px, but they are inert today: the dp step reads only
; font_sizes/ and styles/ and never touches a font, so the entries mark what a later step that
; scales fonts must leave alone. HudTokens holds the colours of ADR 0025 section 13, HudPanel the
; flat panel (no blur, a flat box is cheap on a weak phone),
; AccentRenew and AccentFossil the accent of each side (accent, light and the text on the accent,
; read with get_theme_color by the faction's id). The design's fixed enemy colour #FF9446 is not
; a token. Palette rows: STYLE.md "Palette".
;
; Sizes are dp: HudTheme.gd turns every font size and every StyleBox size (content margins,
; corner radii, border widths, expand margins, shadows, a line's thickness and grow) into px on a
; resize and gives the HUD roots that copy as their theme. Not scaled: a StyleBoxTexture's texture
; margins (they cut the picture, in texture px), the theme's constants (a font's outline_size too:
; layout stays in code, in dp through UiScale) and the StyleBox properties that are not sizes:
; skew (a shear ratio, the same angle on every screen), corner_detail (a count) and
; anti_aliasing_size (the soft edge, 1 px). Scale a constant in HudTheme.scaled() before putting
; one here. An entry that stays in base px is listed in metadata/base_px by its path in this file.
; Type variations (DevButton, NumberLabel, SelectionPanel, EnemyHealth, PerfCard, SidebarTab,
; PowerBar, PowerBarLow, PowerNumber, PowerNumberLow, ItemTile, ItemCost, ItemCostLow, ItemBanner,
; ItemCaption, ItemCaptionWarn, ItemCaptionOn, ItemCaptionDim, OrderLit, ItemSash, StrikeButton, StrikeConfirm, BuildButton, ReadyBadge, HudPanel, CapsButton,
; CapsTitle, CapsBigTitle, EconomyPill, EconomyPillLow, PillWord, AttackTitle, EconomyChipLoss,
; EconomyChipGain, EconomyConsumer, ResultScreen, Scrim, DeployBackdrop, and the pause menu's PauseHud, PauseCard,
; PauseBadge, PauseBadgeFossil, PauseCheck, PauseMuted, PauseButton, PausePrimary,
; PausePrimaryFossil, PauseDanger, PauseStarting, PauseChip, PauseChipFossil, PauseChipOff, the ad banner band's AdCaption, and the menu screens' MenuTitle, SideNameRenew, SideNameFossil, MenuSideCard (Renew, Fossil), MenuSlider (Fossil), MenuToggleRow, MenuToggle (Fossil, Off), MenuTab, MenuTabOn, MenuMapCard (On, Locked), MenuRankBadge, MenuRankLabel and MenuXpBar; P519) are set by
; theme_type_variation on the node, in main.tscn or at build in the script (the power bar's two
; pairs switch with the low-power state, the cost of an item tile with its money).
; The tabs of the build sidebar get their tints from the icon colours of SidebarTab; the glyphs of
; the economy pill (EconomyPill.gd) read HudTokens with get_theme_color.
[gd_resource type="Theme" format=3]

[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://assets/art/fonts/inter/Inter-Regular.ttf" id="1_inter_400"]
[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://assets/art/fonts/inter/Inter-Bold.ttf" id="2_inter_700"]
[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://assets/art/fonts/ibm-plex-mono/IBMPlexMono-Regular.ttf" id="3_plex_400"]
[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://assets/art/fonts/roboto-condensed/RobotoCondensed-Bold.ttf" id="4_roboto_700"]

; The caps faces at the three size classes (Inter Bold for the button, Roboto Condensed Bold for the
; titles): the tracking in whole base px (the font size of each class is under CapsButton, CapsTitle
; and CapsBigTitle below, in dp).
[sub_resource type="FontVariation" id="FontVariation_caps_button"]
